    <!-- Navpill library glyph (siren), 24x24 to match the other navpill icons.

         The inner cut-outs are produced by WINDING, not by a fill rule: every inner
         subpath below is traced opposite to the outer outline, so the nonZero winding
         number cancels to 0 and leaves them transparent.

         This matters because minSdk is 23 and android:fillType only exists from API 24.
         The upstream SVG declares fill-rule="evenodd" and relies on it, but its inner
         subpaths are not consistently wound: two of the three run the same way as the
         outer outline. On API 23 the fillType attribute is ignored and the default nonZero
         rule applies, which rendered those two solid (verified coverage 0.6701 instead of
         0.2951, i.e. a filled blob rather than the outlined siren). The windings here are
         corrected so nonZero and evenOdd produce byte-identical output on every API level.
         Do not normalise the path direction; that silently turns the icon into a blob. -->

